WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.970
Read the hair and scalp before every service.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:07.160
This is the video for module 1 of Hair Care and Simple Styling.

3
00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:14.640
A client says, I want small knotless braids, waist length. A beginner starts parting at once.

4
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.520
A professional first spends about 5 minutes looking at the hair.

5
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.820
Because the same style can be safe on one head and harmful on another.

6
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:31.090
So check the hair, check the scalp, then agree the style, time and price in writing.

7
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:42.940
First, density: how many strands grow on the scalp. Make a part at the crown, hairline, temples and nape, and see how much scalp shows. Temples are often thinnest.

8
00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:53.580
Second, strand width. Hold a shed hair next to sewing thread. Thinner than the thread is fine hair, which breaks easily and needs less added weight.

9
00:00:54.830 --> 00:01:06.220
Third, porosity: how water gets in and out. If sprayed water sits in droplets and dries slowly, porosity is low. If it soaks in and dries fast, it is high.

10
00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:14.360
Fourth, elasticity. Do every check in daylight or with a phone torch, because dim light hides thin temples.

11
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.980
Step 1. Take one wet strand from the back of the head.

12
00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:24.260
Step 2. Hold it firmly near the root, so you do not pull her scalp.

13
00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:36.030
Step 3. Stretch it slowly and gently, then let go. Healthy hair springs back. Hair that snaps at once is brittle. Hair that stays stretched and gummy is weak.

14
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.400
Step 4. Write the result on her card, and never repeat the test on the same strand.

15
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:53.700
For example, Amaka in Enugu has a client, Funmi, who wants small waist-length knotless braids for a wedding. Funmi's hair is fine, with thin temples.

16
00:01:54.950 --> 00:02:09.560
So Amaka recommends medium knotless braids at mid-back length, with no added hair at the temples, and extra drying time because the hair has low porosity. Funmi still gets her braids, in a size her hair can carry.

17
00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:18.600
Check the scalp in good light before you wet or comb. Light white flakes with no redness or pain? Serve, and note it on her card.

18
00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:31.320
Lice or eggs, round scaly patches with broken hairs, pus or sores? Do not serve today. Tell her privately what you saw and suggest a health worker. Never diagnose.

19
00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:41.410
Thin edges mean no tension there. Raw skin means no chemicals and no braiding over it. Wear disposable gloves near broken skin.

20
00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.980
Afterwards, bag every comb, clip and towel you touched.

21
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:53.800
For lice, soak combs in hot water of at least about 54 degrees Celsius for 5 to 10 minutes.

22
00:02:55.050 --> 00:03:01.070
For fungal signs, wash with soap and water, then disinfect as you will learn in module 4.

23
00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.870
Wash your hands for 40 to 60 seconds. And never give medicine or treat a scalp yourself.

24
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:16.840
For example, Chioma in Onitsha plans medium knotless braids: 8 rows of about 10 braids makes 80 braids.

25
00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:23.120
Her own timed average is 6 minutes per braid, so that is 480 minutes.

26
00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.770
She adds 30 minutes for washing and 60 for drying.

27
00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:38.490
Total, 570 minutes, or 9 hours 30 minutes. She writes it down with the price and deposit. Use your own timings, never a guess.

28
00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:50.980
Keep a private card for every visit: her details, your checks, her history, the agreed style, time, price, deposit, and photo consent. For a child, the parent agrees.

29
00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.340
Read it back and ask her to reply agreed on WhatsApp.

30
00:03:55.590 --> 00:04:08.670
To remember. Do the four checks every visit, because hair changes. Fine hair and thin edges need less weight. Postpone and refer privately. Clean every tool. And put time and price in writing.

31
00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:17.550
Now practise. Assess three heads, build your scalp check card and referral list, and hold two practice consultations.

32
00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.850
Continue with the lessons below.
